  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Existing evidence is sparse but points to RNA as the stronger modality: RNA-only PCA single-profile achieves 0.485 validation accuracy and 0.464 F1, while image-only ResNet single-profile is much weaker at 0.208 accuracy and 0.172 F1. The main uncertainty is whether the current RNA-only baseline can be improved by using multiple profiles and a simple aggregation strategy. config_002 tests this by keeping the same promising RNA encoder, pca_n2000, and only extending from single-profile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This is a logical, low-confounding extension of the best current result, and avgpool is preferred over transformer as the simpler baseline aggregation. It is the best next use of budget because it directly clarifies whether profile aggregation matters before investing in more complex multimodal or learned-encoder configurations."
}

